      <title>Compliance Week 2026</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/54356516681901/huge/9b223e4eb084dd9b66196bd1f6c0f822d1465a2c.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Mon, 02 Nov 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>HU Compliance Week 2026</p>

<p>Join the Office of Audit &amp; Compliance (OAC) and our compliance partners across the University in celebrating HU Compliance Week 2026! This annual observance highlights Howard University's commitment to fostering a culture of compliance and upholding an effective compliance program. We also recognize the people, resources, and everyday actions that help us uphold our commitment to integrity, accountability, and excellence in truth and service.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>5 ways to participate in Compliance Week:</p>

<p>1. Complete the Compliance Culture Survey! All faculty and staff are invited to complete the Compliance Culture Survey during HU Compliance Week 2026. Share your perspective and help inform efforts to foster a culture of ethics and compliance at Howard. </p>

<p>2.  Visit the HU Compliance Week 2026 page on the Howard Intranet throughout the week for video messages from compliance partners, announcements, resources, and opportunities to connect with our team. (You can also visit the OAC website to learn more about compliance at Howard.)</p>

<p>3. Take a moment for a policy refresh. Compliance Week is a great time to catch up on University policies, including the new Sanctions and Progressive Discipline Policy. It outlines a consistent approach to addressing policy violations, including missed mandatory training requirements. Use this week to check your assigned training and upcoming deadlines, too!</p>

<p>4. Catch up on your compliance training. Take the opportunity to complete your Title IX/EEO, Cybersecurity, Health Sciences, or other compliance training if you haven’t done so already!</p>

<p>5. Catch us outside! Audit &amp; Compliance team members will be dropping by several campus locations on the OAC Campus Tour, Thursday, November 5th, to share fun giveaways and compliance resources. Stay tuned for updates!</p>

