      <title>Middle States Self-Study Town Hall at  Douglass Hall</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/54356508618143/huge/75832d273a9d5aacb415bf4b3eadba385437f8b2.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Mon, 02 Nov 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>Students, faculty, and staff to participate in a Middle States Self-Study Town Hall on November 2. The session will provide updates on the University’s ongoing self-study process, highlight emerging themes, and offer an opportunity to share feedback as Howard prepares the next draft of its 2027 Self-Study Report, a key component of the University’s reaccreditation application. Community members are encouraged to engage in this important process to reflect on institutional strengths and identify opportunities for continuous improvement.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Date: November 2, 2026
<br>Time: 1:00–2:00 p.m.
<br>Location: Douglass Hall, Room 221</p>

